From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:48:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: limit charging by the
 board's temperature

Name the board-thermal zone to the charger's guard, so a warm board
steps the raised charge currents down.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 95f959787..a2a49a19f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -574,6 +574,8 @@ charger@6b {
 		/* The MT6351 BC1.1 detection module's supply. */
 		linux,guard-usb-detect = "mt6351-usb";
 		linux,guard-charge-voltage-by-temperature;
+		/* The board NTC steps the raised currents down from 47 C. */
+		linux,guard-board-zone = "board-thermal";
 
 		/* VBUS for the left USB-C port as a host; see the ports below. */
 		usb0_vbus: usb-otg-vbus {
-- 
2.43.0

